# 5. Full stationary-cutpoint dictionary

The same construction yields three classical number-theoretic problems.

Let

\[
a_t=(M^t)_{ij}-\frac1n.
\]

Then:

## Exact equality

\[
\exists t:a_t=0
\]

is the Skolem problem for the tangent LRS.

## One-time sign crossing

\[
\exists t:a_t<0
\]

is the complement of Positivity for \(-a_t\) (up to the strict/non-strict convention and finite zero handling).

## Infinitely many sign crossings

\[
\exists^\infty t:a_t<0
\]

is the complement form associated with Ultimate Positivity.

Hence one positive mixing Markov chain at its stationary coordinate threshold contains the classical trinity

\[
\boxed{
\text{Skolem}
\quad
\text{Positivity}
\quad
\text{Ultimate Positivity}.
}
\]

This dictionary is essentially the content of Vahanwala's reachability equivalences, sharpened here by the uniform/doubly-stochastic tangent interpretation.

